# Fork patch files must stay LF in the WORKING TREE as well as in the object
# store. The patches are replayed with `git apply` against a DSH checkout whose
# own .gitattributes enforces `* text=auto eol=lf`, and a context line carrying a
# trailing CR never matches an LF working tree -- measured 2026-09-12: with CRLF
# the whole set failed 0/8 even against its own baseline, with LF it applies 8/8.
#
# Without this rule `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, so the
# fix would survive exactly until the next fresh clone.
*.patch text eol=lf
